From 206a4578428c4f17256adb38782ed059ea74980f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lbarapat <lbarapat@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:25:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] paho-mqtt-c: implement external signing and
 ssl_handshake_thread fixes

Implements the TA-backed mTLS external signing path in MQTTClient.c:

- Register ssl_external_sign_cb as OpenSSL external signing callback
  when ssl_external_signing_method == ENABLE_EXTERNAL_SIGNING
- Spawn ssl_handshake_thread to prevent deadlock when signing callback
  blocks on A2A round-trip (~30 s on PLAT_LV)
- MQTTClient_destroy waits for ssl_handshake_thread to avoid UAF of
  freed SSL context (Paho 1.3.14 heap bug workaround)
- Add poll+retry loop (65 s budget) in ssl_handshake_thread for
  TCPSOCKET_INTERRUPTED after TA A2A signing round-trip
- MQTTClient_connectURIVersion waits for ssl_handshake_thread on timeout
- TOCTOU fix: ListFind guard in MQTTClient_run to detect destroyed client
- Copy struct_version 6 sslopts fields in MQTTClient_connectAll
- Extend connectTimeout to 80 s for TA signing path
- API compat with paho 1.3.14: Thread_* naming, Socket_setWriteAvailable

Signed-off-by: lbarapat <lbarapat@qti.qualcomm.com>
